Part 1 - Undertsand the Business Problem:

1. What is the business problem?
  A grocery store is trying to create a marketing campaign in order to boost sales for their new wine section in the stores. This means
  that the company needs to figure out who they should advertise to in order to maximize profit.  

2. Why is this problem important to the organization?
  This problem is important to the grocery store because if they do not advertise to the right people they will waste money on a 
  marketing campaign. The hope of the campaign is that it will help the company make more money than what will be spent on the campaign 
  and if they do not advertise to the right people they will not meet this goal. Along with this, figuring out who the grocery store
  should advertise to will allow them to decide how they should advertise to them in order to be the most seen and/or persuasive. 

3. Who is affected by this problem?
  The people affected by this problem are the costumers, this is because they will become subject to the advertisments from the marketing
  campaign whether they specifically want to. This will also affect the managers and higher up as they specifically are affected by how
  well the store does in sales. Along with this it will affect employees as if the campaign does not do well they may lose their job or
  recieve a pay cut. The marketing department will be the most affected as they will have to create advertisments meant for these
  specific people in order for the campaign to be effective.


Part 2 - Identify the Data:

1. What data would you need?
  The data that would be needed for this AI system would be the characterisitcs of previous costumers. This includes variables like age,
  income, household number, date costumer started shopping, how recently they shopped at the store, and how much they have spent on wine
  previously. 

2. Where could the data come from?
  The data could come from current members of the grocery store, and the data that the grocery store stores from previous customers.

3. How much historical data might be useful?
  Historical data will be very useful as it shows who their current customers are, and therefore the company should advertise to a 
  similare demographic of people.

4. What would be the most important variables?
  I believe that the most important variables will be the age of the costumers because that is an easy demographic to follow and
  it can be very telling which age group is most likely to buy wine. Another important variable will be the amount of money the 
  customers have already spent on wine in the past. This is because if they have never bought wine before their characteristics will be
  the type that the company would not want to advertise to.

5. What could be missing or inaccurate?
  Something that could be inaccurate is someones age as people lie about their ages online and in their emails very often. Along with
  this someones address or location could be inaccurate if they have moved. 


