Part 4 — Select the AI/ML Approach 

1. Would you use supervised or unsupervised learning?
  This model would use unsupervised learning.

2. Explain your choice.
  This model would use unsupervised learning because it does not already have the answer to the question who should the company
  company advertise to. Instead the model is just compiling data and giving ranges of who is most likely to purchas wine and who will
  be responsive to the marketing campaign. 

3. Would the problem involve classification or prediction?
  This problem would involve prediction not classification.

4. Explain your choice.
  This model would involve prediction because it is trying to predict who the grocery store should advertise to in order to make a
  profit. While it is classifying specific costumers from the data as people who are more likely to buy wine this is not the main 
  objective of the model. The main objective is to identify the characteristics that make someone more susceptable to the marketing.


