Part 6 — Complete AI Solution Summary

Business Problem:
  A grocery store is trying to figure out who to advertise their new wine section to.

Data Needed:
  The data needed to solve this problem is current members of the grocery stores age, family size, annual income, recency of purchase,
  and amount of money spent on wine.

AI/ML Approach:
  This system would be considered machine learning because it is not using complex data.

Type of Learning:
  This system would use unsupervised learning as it is using data without the answers and it would use prediction as it is not trying
  to classify anything.

Model Output:
  The output of the model will be the characteristics of someone who would be a good person to advertise the new wine section to.

Business Benefit:
  This system will help the grocery store as it will help to improve their marketing strategy which will help their sales to increase.

Potential Risk:
  A potential risk of this system is that it has incorrect data and causes the grocery store to advertise to people who will not be 
  interested in the new wine section which could cause the company to not have a profit or not make as much money as possible.


